{
  "_what": "The fields each record kind declares, per format id. There is one entry per id in model.KNOWN_SCHEMAS, which is what a reader ACCEPTS, not what a release shipped: /v2 is here because PREVIOUS_SCHEMAS still accepts it, although no release carried it. tests/test_schema.py asserts that set equality, because the gate reads only the entry for the current SCHEMA and so cannot notice an older one going missing, which is how the two ids releases did ship came to be absent (#249). checks/gate.py refuses a change to the live dataclasses that is not matched here, so adding a field without moving the format id fails the build instead of reaching a reader six hours later (#154, Craig's agent: \"commit a manifest of the format's declared fields, and have checks/gate.py fail when the live Edge, Node or Study fields differ from the manifest while SCHEMA is unchanged\").",
  "_how": "To add a field: move SCHEMA to a new id in model.py, add an entry here for that id, and leave the older entries alone. They are the record of what each released format carried, and an edit to one is a rewrite of history that review should stop. The entries for /v0 and /v1 were reconstructed on 2026-10-11 from the v0.1.0 and v0.2.0 trees, because this file held /v2, which no release ever carried (model.py: \"v2 was never tagged\"), and omitted the two ids that releases did ship, while saying it was the record of released formats; both are still accepted by PREVIOUS_SCHEMAS and are in the published schema's enum. The gate only reads the entry for the current SCHEMA, so nothing noticed (#249).",
